   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Evaluate the following exponential expression: <span data-math=\"4 \\times {8^2} + 2 \\times {8^1} + 7 \\times {8^0}\">4 \\times {8^2} + 2 \\times {8^1} + 7 \\times {8^0}</span>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"4 \\times {8^2} + 2 \\times {8^1} + 7 \\times {8^0}\"></span></p>\n<p>Remember that any base raised to the exponent 0 is 1.</p>\n<p>Use the order of expressions (PEMDAS), which means</p>\n<p>do the exponents first,</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"4 \\times 64 + 2 \\times 8 + 7 \\times 1\"></span></p>\n<p>then multiplications,</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"256 + 16 + 7\"></span></p>\n<p>then additions.</p>\n<p>279</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "279"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
